  title: Frontal Lobe
  description: 'The frontal lobe is the largest part of the brain, located at the
    front, responsible for higher cognitive functions, decision-making, problem-solving,
    and emotional regulation. It plays a crucial role in thinking, behavior, and
    voluntary movement. The frontal lobe is divided into two main regions: the prefrontal
    cortex, which is involved in planning and reasoning, and the motor cortex, which
    coordinates voluntary movements.'
